# M3.5.2 Core local runtime diagnostic — 2026-08-27

## Failure

The first local Core regression invocation used macOS system Python 3.9. It ran
249 discovered tests, then reported seven import errors because the reviewed
`psycopg` dependency is not installed in that interpreter. Core supports Python
3.10+ and CI installs the hash-locked dependency before running tests.

## Impact

No Core or Control file was modified. The failures occurred during test-module
import and are not application assertion failures. Core remained clean at
`dddb94e8ac3d79f6ccd7d696d2fa92da1583850b`.

## Controlled resolution

Use an already-configured supported project interpreter if present. Do not
modify the macOS system interpreter. If no project runtime exists, the exact
green GitHub Core CI for the unchanged SHA is the authoritative regression
evidence; M3.5.2's changed Control artifacts remain covered by their own local
and remote suites.
